# Far copy, step 25.8 (7.2.46): the reader of the common file in language 4 with the link 2 (see far_copy_file_w.tw, the writer). It reads the cells of the writer: 32 bits at the byte 0,
# 8 bits at the byte 3, 64 bits at the byte 8: `copy &y 0x2...` waits for the flag of the cell (polls it, up to 2^18 failed polls), then reads the data; when the flag does not come
# the data are all ones (the prohibitive price) and the program goes on. The cells (a, b, c) go to stderr at the end.
:a data 32 0
:b data 8 0
:c data 64 0
:main block
copy &a 0x200000002000000000000000000000000
copy &b 0x200000002000000000000000000000018
copy &c 0x200000002000000000000000000000040
warn &a
warn &b
warn &c
halt
